agp
Inspect a local AGP node. Enter a context, then use show or ls.
  advertisements/  Received advertisements and their source sessions.
  configuration/  Effective redacted node configuration.
  connections/  Display connection identities, states, supplied uptime and hold TTL.
  counters/  Canonical operational counters.
  endpoints/  Locally registered endpoints and binding identities.
  forwarding/  Resolved forwarding entries.
  health/  Node lifecycle, readiness, and identity.
  resources/  Resource usage and observed high-water marks.
  routes/  Display route candidates and supplied selected-route membership.
  snapshot/  Summary of one canonical operations capture; --json retains all sections.
  advertisements.list [connected:json-http-get-v1]
    Received advertisements and their source sessions.
    Endpoint: --url <loopback-url> or AGP_MANAGEMENT_URL; granted: true
    Output view: advertisements (use --table)
  configuration.list [connected:json-http-get-v1]
    Effective redacted node configuration.
    Endpoint: --url <loopback-url> or AGP_MANAGEMENT_URL; granted: true
    Output view: configuration (use --table)
  connections.list [connected:json-http-get-v1]
    Display connection identities, states, supplied uptime and hold TTL.
    Endpoint: --url <loopback-url> or AGP_MANAGEMENT_URL; granted: true
    Output view: connections (use --table)
  counters.list [connected:json-http-get-v1]
    Canonical operational counters.
    Endpoint: --url <loopback-url> or AGP_MANAGEMENT_URL; granted: true
    Output view: counters (use --table)
  endpoints.list [connected:json-http-get-v1]
    Locally registered endpoints and binding identities.
    Endpoint: --url <loopback-url> or AGP_MANAGEMENT_URL; granted: true
    Output view: endpoints (use --table)
  forwarding.list [connected:json-http-get-v1]
    Resolved forwarding entries.
    Endpoint: --url <loopback-url> or AGP_MANAGEMENT_URL; granted: true
    Output view: forwarding (use --table)
  health.list [connected:json-http-get-v1]
    Node lifecycle, readiness, and identity.
    Endpoint: --url <loopback-url> or AGP_MANAGEMENT_URL; granted: true
    Output view: health (use --table)
  resources.list [connected:json-http-get-v1]
    Resource usage and observed high-water marks.
    Endpoint: --url <loopback-url> or AGP_MANAGEMENT_URL; granted: true
    Output view: resources (use --table)
  routes.list [connected:json-http-get-v1]
    Display route candidates and supplied selected-route membership.
    Endpoint: --url <loopback-url> or AGP_MANAGEMENT_URL; granted: true
    Output view: routes (use --table)
  snapshot.list [connected:json-http-get-v1]
    Summary of one canonical operations capture; --json retains all sections.
